        "sha": "d69f78a7862c4af339de015625987b506f8e0a2b",
        "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/bitcoin-core/secp256k1/git/trees/d69f78a7862c4af339de015625987b506f8e0a2b"
      },
      "verification": {
        "verified": true,
        "reason": "valid",
        "payload": "tree d69f78a7862c4af339de015625987b506f8e0a2b\nparent 738675267106b91dd9070a00c201825dd2440c64\nauthor Ferdinando Ametrano <ferdinando@ametrano.net> 1792655281 +0200\ncommitter Ferdinando Ametrano <ferdinando@ametrano.net> 1792662745 +0200\n\nsilentpayments: add API function for scanning with a list of labels\n\nAdd `secp256k1_silentpayments_recipient_scan_outputs_with_labels`. It\ntakes the labels as an array of label entries (label and label tweak)\ninstead of a label lookup callback, and finds the same outputs as\n`_recipient_scan_outputs`.\n\nFor each k it adds every label to unlabeled_output and compares the x\ncoordinates of the results with the tx outputs. This costs one point\naddition per label instead of two per tx output, and needs no label\nlookups. It needs no sorting, no scratch space and no heap allocation,\nand it does not modify its inputs.\n\nThe results match those of `_recipient_scan_outputs` also for malformed\ntransactions: the tx output with the lowest index wins, then a direct\nmatch over a label match, then the label candidate with even Y over the\none with odd Y.\n",
        "signature": "-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niJEEABYKADkWIQRJ5SMZs3eEinN+Lb4iedqLwmlHIAUCatnc2RsUgAAAAAAEAA5t\nYW51MiwyLjUrMS4xMiwwLDMACgkQInnai8JpRyB3ygD+PzZhASCbPoiimpVMbRWC\nB2dryEdD1nklGIv76GhPpH4BAMp7XHt/bxSaFFIN6DZr0PnsnT4EdVvKJFsUaEv/\n4bgK\n=KFzi\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----"
